{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "רחובות", :translit "rehovot", :gloss "broad places"} {:he "יון", :translit "yavan", :gloss "Greece"} {:he "ופרינו בארץ", :translit "ufrinu va'aretz", :gloss "and we shall be fruitful in the land"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "רחובות", :b "יון"}], :frame {:text "The verse 'and we shall be fruitful in the land' (Genesis 26:22) is read as a prophecy of national survival. The Yavan/Greek decrees targeted key mitzvot: Bereshit Rabbah 16:5 lists circumcision, Shabbat, and Torah study; Megillat Antiochus narrates that they banned circumcision and Shabbat. The link between ritual immersion and fertility draws on the talmudic principle that a convert immerses to enter the covenant (Yevamot 47b).", :sources ["Genesis 26:22" "Bereshit Rabbah 16:5" "Megillat Antiochus" "Yevamot 47b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "רחובות", :a-value 622, :b "יון", :b-value 66, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:20.871933722Z", :model "glm-5.2"}